{
 "_doc": "Tier-1 set piece: the Lift 3 crash site (DESIGN \u00a71 and \u00a711), the Remand Salvage Program lift the player came in on, down in the timber short of the drop. The main map stands it about 0.7 km east of the drop site (d6_larch_hollow region.json, back along the approach); random worlds place it near their drop the same way (World's generator). Mostly outdoors: a long swath of snapped trunks and scorched ground (plan rows 20..53) leading to the burned-out forward fuselage, which reuses the Cordon transport wreck's props (data/props/wild4_plane.json): the w4_plane_fuselage_fwd shell wraps kit rooms on exactly the rectangle and outside openings its catalog cuts (tools/assetgen/blender_catalogs/props_wild4_plane.py SHELLS; here cols 12..15, rows 5..18: crew bay rows 5..8 with the flight deck over it on level 1, reached by a ladder through a hatch, the cargo hold rows 9..18 open over the ramp lip), w4_plane_nose in the bank north of it, the tail cone, one wing and the dead number two engine back in the swath. No Hollowed, no traps: the crew are remains (corpse_remains), the loot is early gear (loot tables lift3_*: cloth, a bottle, a light, a little food). Route: the swath -> the engine and the tail -> the debris field (canisters, stores, the wing) -> the torn end and over the lip -> the hold's empty seats (the seat-back) -> the crew bay's salvager seats -> up the ladder: the flight deck, the kneeboard card, the manifest, the captain's kit (the loot room) -> out the blown emergency exit. Alternatives: where the first officer lies, where the one chute came down, whether the hold still smoulders. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
