   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "story": "Lift 3 was a Remand Salvage Program aircraft, flown out of Waystation 9 by Capt. N. Whitlock and F/O J. Iredale with one salvager aboard where three were manifested: No. 4466 had died in holding before dawn and No. 4479 had cut off the tether and missed muster. It crossed the firebreak at first light with a rack of supply canisters for the drop. Over the timber the ground moved with no wind, the number two engine rolled back, and Whitlock could not hold height on one. It went in short of the drop through a long swath of trees, lost its tail and a wing, ploughed its nose into a bank and burned. The salvager in seat 1 walked out of the torn end with the tether ticking and went on toward the drop on foot. The crew did not. The wreck burned out before first light, and nobody came for it.",
